WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.594
REFINERY makes process decisions inspectable.

00:00:03.594 --> 00:00:15.256
This is a working CPU prototype with a synthetic refinery unit, six logical process loops, observation-based diagnosis, and conditional forecasts.

00:00:15.256 --> 00:00:18.691
It is not connected to operating equipment.

00:00:18.691 --> 00:00:23.124
[Actual CPU calculation: 113.9 seconds; middle of waiting omitted.]
First, choose a configuration and a simulated disturbance.

00:00:23.124 --> 00:00:27.558
Here we request cooling loss and enable action comparison.

00:00:27.558 --> 00:00:39.482
The service calculates a normal reference and disturbed trajectory, checks physical balances, diagnoses from observations, and evaluates possible responses.

00:00:39.482 --> 00:00:43.048
The accepted result appears across the workspace.

00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:50.544
Expand all displays every equipment temperature and pressure together with the corresponding reference.

00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:55.784
This demonstration uses simulated measurements, not a live plant stream.

00:00:55.784 --> 00:01:04.066
The diagnostic view explains the selected cooling-loss hypothesis using measured residuals and a causal chain.

00:01:04.066 --> 00:01:06.475
Other hypotheses remain visible.

00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:10.315
Similarity scores are not calibrated probabilities.

00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:16.490
Hidden scenario labels are reserved for outcome verification, after the diagnosis.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:24.458
What-if analysis compares holding the current settings, restoring cooling, reducing heat, and reducing feed.

00:01:24.458 --> 00:01:29.254
These are conditional predictions under stated model assumptions.

00:01:29.254 --> 00:01:33.016
The interface issues no commands to real equipment.

00:01:33.016 --> 00:01:41.710
The video wall brings loop summaries, equipment states, colored histograms, events, and trends into one large-screen view.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:47.909
Engineers can review the latest accepted calculation without opening each loop in turn.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:54.992
Reports retain the result identifier, model version, and mass and energy balance evidence.

00:01:54.992 --> 00:01:58.770
CSV and JSON exports support independent review.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:07.585
The public package includes source code, a frozen synthetic model bundle, and reproducible startup instructions.

00:02:07.585 --> 00:02:13.664
This is an engineering prototype, not an industrially qualified safety system.

00:02:13.664 --> 00:02:20.133
The separate research diagnostics and their frozen results are preserved privately.

